WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of my favorite
things, of course,

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.303
is sketches that are written
that do not make it to the show,

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-And some of these ideas maybe

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
have not even been written.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.010
-Do you have some favorites?
-Even the ones that have been

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
written haven't really been
written.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've been like really,
half thought out.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What is
the Rosetta Stone sketch?

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was when Donald Trump
hosted.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.321
I pitched him an idea that he
weirdly didn't want to do,

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:26.126
where he was the spokesman
for Rosetta Stone Mexican.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he would teach you phrases
you could say to someone

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was Mexican, like,
"You're gonna build the wall."

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:36.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I see.
-No -- no, usted are.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, whatever.
-Usted are.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:43.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was heroin A.M.?
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.478 line:92%
-That was non-drowsy heroin.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.246 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:49.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was from the makers
of cocaine P.M.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:54.754
And it was a sketch that was not
popular in middle America.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.690
-Some sketches are just good
ideas and it's not even funny.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.726
-Yeah, that's a great product.
-That's just a good product.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You want to take heroin,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you also want to get some
stuff done.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.900
-What was -- was it your idea
the origin of screw the pooch?

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.637
-Yeah. I wanted to do a sketch
about the first guy to ever say

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
the phrase "screwed the pooch"
because an intern one time

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.210 line:92%
messed up a coffee order,

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"hey, I didn't order this."

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes, "I'm sorry
about that, Che.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really screwed the pooch
on that one."

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "what was that?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes,
"screwed the pooch.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.656
It means I made a mistake."
And I was like "no, man,

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
it means, you had sex
with a dog."

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
"And you should probably stop
saying that

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a workplace environment."
So I wanted to just dig

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:41.434
into that guy, because I'm sure
he probably had sex with a dog

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.104 size:81% position:41%
one time and just kept
pretending that it was

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
a mistake that everybody else
makes.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.375
-Yeah, that's like the coffee
thing. We all make mistakes.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you messed up the coffee?
Now who has sex with dogs?

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.982
Still you, Gary! You're still
the only one that's done that.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Half Viagra?
-Oh, yeah. That's a fun one.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we kept seeing
these ads -- I don't know

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you've seen them --
for single packs of Viagra.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:05.525
Where it's like a weird husband,
and it's, like, "we're going on

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
a trip with my wife"
and he's like,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
"oh, we'll pack one single
pack of Viagra."

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.897 line:92%
He's like, "I want to have sex,

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I don't want to carry
the whole bottle."

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Right.
-You know, so on vacation,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can be like,
"you get one shot."

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:19.372
But we wanted to do ads
for half-packs of Viagra.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.475
And if you didn't want to have
sex, you just wanted to make it

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
look a little bigger.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like if you knew you were
going somewhere,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.783 size:84% position:42%
like you had a doctor's
appointment, you know?

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.652
-Or like a tailor or something.
You know --

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wanna...Got to use like,
a stadium urinal.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want people to be...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.725 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know?
-Yeah.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:44.364
Whatever. I still say we should
have called it Viagra al dente.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First black guy to boo
Jackie Robinson?

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Right.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.743 line:92%
First of all, it was February,

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wanted
a black history sketch.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:58.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-And I was like,

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.614
"who was the first black guy to
boo Jackie Robinson

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.516 size:78% position:39%
for a baseball play?"
There had to be one.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.252 size:84% position:42%
I mean, he -- I'm sure
he had an error before.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:09.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-Yeah. Censor said no.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:12.926
-Really?
-Yeah, my favorite sketches are,

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, really racially charged.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:18.198
-Like Chris Hemsworth hosted,
and I wanted to do a sketch

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.466
where the Avengers save the day,
but in the process,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thor accidentally kills
an unarmed black teenager.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:28.708 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He didn't think that was
on brand?

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:33.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he said it wouldn't
help with tickets.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.381 size:75% position:38%
-I think it would've
helped with tickets.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought it would help
with tickets, too.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.087 size:84% position:42%
-You had a -- Was it
a CVS game show sketch?

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:45.758
-A game show that was set inside
of a CVS that was called

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Who Works Here?"

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's a good one.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.965
-Contestants had to buzz in
and try and decide is that

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:55.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, an employee,
or a drifter in a red vest?

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, this one you guys
should've done.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:02.342
Cecilia Gimenez was a character
that Kate McKinnon played.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:02.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Yes.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And for the actual news story
when she first played him,

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was a painting
of Jesus, right?

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...that someone repainted...

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.584
-Yeah.
-And then, like, to retouch it,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it looked like
a howler monkey.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Basically.
-It was, like, the worst

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
repainting job of all time.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we did one I think
where she did

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Cristiano Ronaldo statue
that was in segment two.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.029
-Yeah.
-Or the Lucy one -- it was like

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:25.932
a Lucille Ball where she looked
like the snake character

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "Beetlejuice."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this, someone talked about
'cause they saw --

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you guys saw
the animatronic Trump

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:35.575
at Disney World or something...
-Frightening.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...where she was the one who
designed that.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:40.046 size:88% position:44%
It basically looked like
a way worse Jon Voight.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Melty Voight.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:46.653
So what is the pressure like?
Obviously, every week on "SNL,"

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:47.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
there is a certain amount
of pressure.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys have one
of the all-time greats,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will Ferrell, this week.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some would say, oh, my God,
cruise control,

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:56.329
but you have to feel pressure.
-Yeah. You do, you feel a lot

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.699
of pressure 'cause everyone
already knows he's good.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if it's not good,
it's our fault.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.072 size:81% position:41%
We're the ones that's
the problem, so, yeah,

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.073 size:84% position:42% line:92%
it's a lot of pressure.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hopefully Will can step up
to it.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.477 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
Carry us through
with a cowbell, too.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:17.383
-Well, I especially am grateful
you guys came here tonight

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.619
because pretty much you're gonna
leave here and you're gonna go

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
right upstairs...
-Yeah.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.089
-...and write through the night.
I can't wait for Saturday.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always such a pleasure
to see both of you.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.858
-Thank you for having us.
-And "Update" has been

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.127 size:84% position:42%
so fantastic this year.
Keep up the great work.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.028 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Ah, thank you, man.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations
on the Globes, too.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were fantastic
hosting the Globes.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
Really appreciate it.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:36.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wonderful.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.206
-Jost -- Jost sent me jokes for
the Globes, which was very nice,

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:44.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
and like a day before
the Globes, you had an idea.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-It was unproduceable.

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah, I wanted Andy Samberg

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play the creature
from "The Shape of Water."

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.618
[ Laughter ]
And that he was in the audience

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was falling in love
with Seth as the show went on.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:06:00.059
And the second time you saw him,
he was in a bathtub on stage

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
asking Seth to get in
the bathtub.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:03.029 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:06.132
-And it was great 'cause it
was written like someone who had

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:08.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
never been in show business.
-Yes.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how I try to approach
every idea.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You had the good sense to do

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:15.675
like, good, "smart stuff."
-No, no, no, I -- but I did like

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
the idea of like, just
constantly, like,

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the middle of, like,
a speech.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like Oprah giving her speech,
Andy being like,

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:22.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I need water!"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.951 size:78% position:39%
I think that was what
the evening needed.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You definitely should have
booed Oprah.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
That would've been the best.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:30.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, what?
-Get Seth back out!

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:31.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you guys so much
for being here.

